// daycard.templ — C-CALV4-DAYCARD (calendar-v4 round 2, slice R2-2a): the day
// card's SCAFFOLD and the event editor's.
//
// ONE CARD PER PAGE, NOT ONE PER BLOCK ([DC-3] SIGNED). The Bench stacks N
// Blocks; N cards would be N popovers, N listeners and N payload copies, and
// "the card and the Ledger cannot disagree" would stop being checkable in one
// place. This is the singleton, positioned per click from the clicked cell's
// getBoundingClientRect() — CSS anchor positioning would need a unique
// anchor-name on every day cell, i.e. an edit to instrument.templ, which is the
// one thing this slice's §1 forbids.
//
// [popover] IS THE MECHANISM, AND IT IS LOAD-BEARING. `.cal-block-host .block`
// clips (calendar-block.css:493-501), so a positioned box inside the grid is
// cut off by the Block's own overflow. The top layer escapes that WITHOUT
// touching the Block — which is the whole shape of this slice: read the Block's
// DOM, listen to it, mount beside it, mutate nothing inside it.
//
// THE ROWS ARE BUILT BY THE MODULE; THE CONTROLS ARE BUILT HERE. That split is
// [DC-9] SIGNED, not a convenience. A day's rows change per click and rendering
// N days x N calendars of markup for one day's reading is what the page payload
// exists to avoid — but EVERY ROLE GATE IS MARKUP-LEVEL, decided by the
// producer, never by CSS and never by JS. So `+ New event`, the GM-only
// control, the type picker and `Delete` are either IN THIS FILE for this viewer
// or they are absent from their DOM entirely. There is no disabled state and no
// `title` explaining an absence: permission is ABSENCE (WG-spec V18, and P9's
// LYR-9 item 5 adopting it product-wide where a wave already touches).
//
// GUARD B4: every dated node here carries `data-day` in the dayKey namespace.
// The card head carries it empty on the wire and the module fills it at open,
// which is the same contract the rows are built under.

package calendar

// dayCardScaffold is the page-level card. Rendered once by bench.templ, outside
// every .cal-block-host, and only when there is a payload to open it on.
//
// popover="manual", NOT "auto", AND THE REASON IS THE REGISTER. `auto` gives
// light-dismiss and Escape for free, but both close the popover SYNCHRONOUSLY
// through the UA — the hiding `beforetoggle` is not cancelable — so the
// register's 160ms close would run on the button path and be skipped on every
// other one. One grammar means one close, so the module owns dismissal (Escape,
// and a pointerdown outside the card) and every path leaves the same way.
templ dayCardScaffold(m DayCardMount) {
	<div
		id="cal-daycard"
		class="cal-daycard"
		popover="manual"
		data-cal-daycard
		data-campaign-id={ m.CampaignID }
		if m.CanCreate {
			data-dc-can-edit
		}
		aria-labelledby="cal-daycard-head"
	>
		<div class="dcbox" data-dc-box>
			<h2 class="dc-h" id="cal-daycard-head" data-dc-head data-day=""></h2>
			<div class="dc-rows" data-dc-rows></div>
			<p class="dc-empty" data-dc-empty hidden>No events on this day.</p>
			<div class="dc-f" data-dc-foot>
				// The module inserts `Open in the Ledger` before this button when
				// the payload says the column is docked; the button itself is
				// server-gated and the module never creates or removes it.
				if m.CanCreate {
					<button type="button" class="dc-door" data-dc-new>+ New event</button>
				}
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
}


// dayCardEditor is the event editor, and C-CALV4-EDITOR-R2b turns the stage-2
// MECHANISM into the chrome the 22 sealed stills draw.
//
// WHAT CHANGED, AND WHAT DELIBERATELY DID NOT. Stage 2 shipped a `<select>` for
// the type, three number inputs for the date and a checkbox for GM-only. Every
// one of those controls is REPLACED here and every one of their `data-de-*`
// HANDLES SURVIVES ([ER-10] SIGNED, condition 1): a picker that replaces
// `<select data-de-category>` carries `data-de-category` on the node the module
// reads. The request bodies are byte-equivalent for equivalent input (condition
// 2) and every amended assertion is named, commented and mutation-tested
// (condition 3). Restyle the control; keep the handle; keep the body.
//
// ZERO NEW WRITE ROUTES, STILL ([DC-8] SIGNED, unchanged). Create is POST
// /campaigns/:id/calendars/:calId/events (Scribe), update is PUT
// .../events/:eid (Scribe), delete is DELETE .../events/:eid (Owner), and the
// tie picker READS GET /campaigns/:id/entities/search. All of them shipped
// before this slice; routes_snapshot.txt is untouched.
//
// ── EVERY GATE IS MARKUP-LEVEL, AND THE CHROME IS WHERE THAT BECOMES VISIBLE ─
//
// [DC-9] SIGNED, restated because this is the first surface where the two axes
// are drawn side by side:
//
//	the ◥ DM only card   CanAuthorDmOnly() — the CAPABILITY, not the role
//	the ◈ Restricted card + the audience roster   CanRestrict (Owner)
//	Delete                                        CanDelete (Owner), and
//	                                              ABSENT ON A DRAFT
//
// THE CARD SET IS THE GATE SET, AND `<2` CARDS MEANS THE FIELDSET IS GONE. A
// Scribe with neither capability has exactly one lawful visibility, so there is
// no choice to render: not a radio group of one, not a collapsed row, not a
// sentence saying why. Gone. `editor-scribe-light.png` is that state.
//
// THE VISIBILITY CARDS ARE REAL RADIOS AND THAT IS LOAD-BEARING. A `<button
// aria-pressed>` group would need JS for keyboard traversal, would need JS to
// stay mutually exclusive, and would put `data-de-gmonly`'s checkedness — which
// the write path reads and five test files pin — behind a script. A radio group
// gives arrow-key traversal, exclusivity and `.checked` for free, so the
// module's read is the SAME read it always was.
//
// ── WHAT IS ABSENT, AND WHY EACH ABSENCE IS A DECISION ─────────────────────
//
//   - THE `year` RECURRENCE UNIT. `recurrence_type` accepts exactly weekly,
//     biweekly, monthly and custom (model.go:214-217); OccursOn sends anything
//     else to `default: return onBase` (model.go:305-309). A wrong unit is not
//     an error, it is a SILENT SINGLE OCCURRENCE — so an unbacked unit in a
//     picker is a trap, and the one thing worse than a missing option is one
//     that quietly does nothing. The mockup offers `year` UNCHIPPED; it does
//     not ship at all.
//   - THE RECURRENCE "ENDS" CYCLER. RecurrenceEnd* and RecurrenceMaxOccurrences
//     exist on the model and NEITHER the shipped POST nor the shipped PUT binds
//     any of them (handler.go), which is why eventEditorRecord leaves them off.
//     A control with no write path and no signed design is ABSENT, not chipped:
//     a chip is a promise addressed to someone who can act on it.
//   - THE OWNER ROW. No API field, no signed design. Absence, not a chip.
//   - THE KNOWLEDGE-HORIZON FOOT under the date grid. The drawing chips it;
//     there is no queryable horizon on main and it is not in §5's table.
//   - THE `.hint` RATIONALE STRINGS. Design rationale addressed to a reviewer,
//     rendered inside the product, is a REVIEW [POLICY] finding. Zero, asserted.
//   - THE PREVIEW'S "WHO SEES IT" ROSTER. It resolves a COMPOSED audience that
//     does not exist on main (there is no member_tags table); that is W-G's.
//   - `+ tie another` AND THE MULTI-TIE LIST. The primary tie is `entity_id`,
//     which BOTH shipped writes bind and the record round-trips. The multi-tie
//     rides three more routes and a list this slice's stills draw as one pill;
//     [ER-4] SIGNED makes shipping the single tie with remove the sanctioned
//     shape and books the rest.
//
// THE EDITOR IS NOT RENDERED AT ALL BELOW THE SCRIBE FLOOR. bench.templ gates
// the whole component, so a player's page contains no editor scaffold, no field
// names, no route strings and the literal `needs backend` zero times.
templ dayCardEditor(m DayCardMount) {
	<div
		id="cal-dayeditor"
		class="cal-dayeditor"
		popover="manual"
		data-cal-dayeditor
		data-campaign-id={ m.CampaignID }
		if m.CanRestrict {
			data-de-can-restrict
		}
		aria-labelledby="cal-dayeditor-head"
	>
		<div class="dcbox" data-dc-box>
			// THE HEAD RESTATES THE EVENT'S TYPE IN THREE CHANNELS, NOT ONE. The
			// 3px bar carries the hue; `.tymark` directly under it carries the
			// same type's STROKE PATTERN and its GLYPH. The stills index measured
			// the old proximity claim at 99px with three controls interposed and
			// replaced the argument with structure — the measured gap is 13.3px
			// worst case, and it is structural here for the same reason.
			//
			// `--accent` NEVER INKS THIS BAR. It takes the event's own --axis,
			// which the module writes from the payload's normalised token.
			<div class="ed-bar" data-de-bar aria-hidden="true"></div>
			<div class="ed-head">
				<span class="tymark" data-de-tymark aria-hidden="true">
					<i class="rail p1" data-de-tyrail></i>
					<span class="g" data-de-tyglyph></span>
				</span>
				<h2 class="dc-h t" id="cal-dayeditor-head" data-de-head data-day=""></h2>
				<span class="sp"></span>
				// The record's own id, or `draft` before the POST has returned
				// one. It is a readout, never a control.
				<span class="readout mono" data-de-id></span>
				// `.ed-head .btn{flex:none}` in the sheet: adding the type mark
				// made this the item that gave way and it measured 23.4px at 390.
				// The shrink belongs on the label, which is the only thing in this
				// row that should carry it.
				<button type="button" class="btn xs ghost" data-de-cancel aria-label="Close the editor">✕</button>
			</div>
			<form class="de-form" data-de-form>
				// TWO COLUMNS ABOVE THE BREAKPOINT, ONE BELOW ([ER-5] SIGNED).
				// The breakpoint is a hard requirement, not a nicety, and the
				// desktop width is MEASURED against the clear band placeCard can
				// actually find rather than taken from the drawing.
				<div class="ed-body">
					<div class="ed-form-col">
						<div class="fld">
							<label class="de-lab" for="de-name">Title</label>
							<input class="in" type="text" id="de-name" name="name" data-de-name required maxlength="200"/>
						</div>
						// THE TYPE RAIL IS THE LOCKED TRIPLE: hue rail + stroke
						// pattern + glyph, one .topt per category. The GLYPH IS
						// INKED --text-body AND NEVER --axis — the stills index
						// measured 2.27:1 and 3.06:1 on axis-inked glyphs and
						// retired both sites by name. The rail beside it carries
						// the hue, so the option keeps all three channels.
						//
						// Seeded from the PAGE PAYLOAD, per calendar, because
						// GET /calendars/:calId/event-categories sits behind an
						// OWNER floor a Scribe cannot reach ([DC-8](c) option ii).
						//
						// `data-de-category` SURVIVES ON THE NODE THE MODULE READS
						// ([ER-10] condition 1). It moved from the <select> to a
						// hidden input; the module still reads `.value` and the
						// request body is byte-identical for the same choice.
						<div class="fld">
							<span class="de-lab">Type</span>
							<div class="types" data-de-typerail role="radiogroup" aria-label="Event type"></div>
							<input type="hidden" name="category" data-de-category/>
						</div>
						<div class="fld">
							<label class="de-lab" for="de-desc">Description</label>
							<textarea class="in prose" id="de-desc" name="description" data-de-desc rows="3"></textarea>
						</div>
						// THE REAL MONTH GRID. Its week length is the CALENDAR'S
						// OWN, derived by the module from the payload's weekday
						// names — there is no literal 7 and no literal 10 anywhere
						// in this file, the sheet or the module. The intercalary
						// day is a FULL-WIDTH ROW and a REAL DATE: Midwinter 1 is
						// not Deepwinter 1, it lives in its own is_intercalary
						// month, and the payload carries both key namespaces so
						// the editor writes the coordinates the API takes.
						//
						// The three number inputs stage 2 shipped are now hidden
						// fields the grid drives. Their handles are unchanged.
						<div class="fld">
							<span class="de-lab" data-de-datelab>Date</span>
							<div class="dp" data-de-datepicker></div>
							<span class="readout" data-de-dateread></span>
							<input type="hidden" name="year" data-de-year/>
							<input type="hidden" name="month" data-de-month/>
							<input type="hidden" name="day" data-de-day/>
						</div>
						<div class="frow frow-split">
							// IN-WORLD TIME CARRIES NO CHIP. start_hour /
							// start_minute / end_hour / end_minute are shipped
							// columns with shipped bindings — the mockup's
							// `needs backend` chip over this field was simply
							// wrong and it comes off rather than being ported.
							<div class="fld">
								<label class="de-lab de-inline">
									<input type="checkbox" data-de-allday checked/>
									<span>All day</span>
								</label>
								<div class="frow de-time" data-de-timerow hidden>
									<span class="readout">from</span>
									<input class="in num" type="number" data-de-starth aria-label="Start hour" min="0" step="1" placeholder="hh"/>
									<span class="readout">:</span>
									<input class="in num" type="number" data-de-startm aria-label="Start minute" min="0" step="1" placeholder="mm"/>
									<span class="readout">to</span>
									<input class="in num" type="number" data-de-endh aria-label="End hour" min="0" step="1" placeholder="hh"/>
									<span class="readout">:</span>
									<input class="in num" type="number" data-de-endm aria-label="End minute" min="0" step="1" placeholder="mm"/>
								</div>
							</div>
							// ENDS ON — end_year / end_month / end_day, all three
							// shipped. THE END DATE MAY NEVER PRECEDE ITS START:
							// the module cycles it over the month's OWN ordered
							// date list, on which the intercalary day is simply
							// the last entry, so a start ON that day offers no end
							// options at all rather than clamping backwards.
							<div class="fld">
								<span class="de-lab">Ends</span>
								<button type="button" class="in sel-like" data-end-pick data-de-endread>ends the same day <span class="ar" aria-hidden="true">⌄</span></button>
								<input type="hidden" data-de-endyear/>
								<input type="hidden" data-de-endmonth/>
								<input type="hidden" data-de-endday/>
							</div>
						</div>
						// RECURRENCE, WITH THE UNIT LIST CORRECTED IN BOTH
						// DIRECTIONS. §5 and the mockup both chip the week unit as
						// invention: they are wrong. Week-based recurrence strides
						// `WeekLength() × recurrenceWeeks(...)`, so on a ten-day
						// calendar `weekly` MEANS every tenday and the chip comes
						// OFF. The mockup offers `year` unchipped: there is no
						// yearly type, it degrades silently, and it does not ship.
						// What stays chipped is `day` and the moon unit — neither
						// is an accepted recurrence_type — and the day-of-week
						// multi-select, because expansion is BASE-ANCHORED and
						// ignores recurrence_day_of_week entirely (.ai.md:963).
						// Every recurrence control is GM-side by construction: a
						// player has no editor to meet one in.
						<div class="fld" data-de-recurrence>
							<span class="de-lab">Recurrence</span>
							<div class="frow">
								<span class="seg" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Recurrence">
									<button type="button" data-rec-pick="once" aria-pressed="true">Once</button>
									<button type="button" data-rec-pick="repeats" aria-pressed="false">Repeats</button>
								</span>
								<span class="rec-on" data-de-recon hidden>
									<span class="readout">every</span>
									<input class="in num" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="1" data-de-recevery aria-label="Recurrence interval"/>
									<span class="units" data-de-recunits role="radiogroup" aria-label="Recurrence unit"></span>
								</span>
								<span class="readout" data-de-recread></span>
							</div>
							<div class="recbox" data-de-recbox hidden>
								<span class="cap">
									On days of the week
									<span class="badge need">needs backend</span>
								</span>
								<div class="wdpick" data-de-wdpick></div>
							</div>
						</div>
						if m.CanAuthorDmOnly || m.CanRestrict {
							// THE FIELDSET EXISTS ONLY WHEN THERE ARE TWO CARDS TO
							// CHOOSE BETWEEN, and that is a CONSEQUENCE of the gates
							// rather than a fourth decision. Public is every author's;
							// the other two are their own capabilities.
							<div class="fld" data-de-visibility>
								<span class="de-lab">
									Visibility
									<span class="badge gm">GM</span>
								</span>
								<div class="vis" data-de-vis>
									<label class="viscard">
										<input type="radio" class="vh" name="de-vis" value="public" data-vis-pick="public" checked/>
										<span class="nm">Public</span>
										<span class="sub">every member of the campaign sees it</span>
									</label>
									if m.CanAuthorDmOnly {
										// The server DOWNGRADES dm_only to everyone for
										// anyone without CanAuthorDmOnly (handler.go), so
										// offering this to a plain Scribe would be offering
										// a switch the server silently ignores.
										<label class="viscard">
											<input type="radio" class="vh" name="de-vis" value="gmonly" data-vis-pick="gmonly" data-de-gmonly/>
											<span class="nm"><span class="gold" aria-hidden="true">◥</span> DM only</span>
											<span class="sub">you and the GMs — the grid gets the gold dogear</span>
										</label>
									}
									if m.CanRestrict {
										// PUT .../events/:eid/visibility is Owner-floor, so
										// the card AND the roster it draws from are Owner's.
										<label class="viscard">
											<input type="radio" class="vh" name="de-vis" value="restricted" data-vis-pick="restricted" data-de-restricted/>
											<span class="nm"><span class="gold" aria-hidden="true">◈</span> Restricted</span>
											<span class="sub">only the members you allow</span>
											<span class="audmark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
										</label>
									}
								</div>
								if m.CanRestrict {
									<div class="audb" data-de-aud hidden>
										<span class="cap">Who this is restricted to</span>
										<div class="audrows" data-de-audrows></div>
									</div>
								}
							</div>
						}
						// entity_id on create and update — both shipped writes bind
						// it and eventEditorRecord round-trips it. The picker READS
						// GET /campaigns/:id/entities/search, which is a cross-plugin
						// FETCH and not a cross-plugin IMPORT: check-plugin-isolation
						// polices Go imports, and a client-side call to another
						// plugin's public API breaks nothing.
						<div class="fld" data-de-tie>
							<label class="de-lab" for="de-tiesearch">Tied to</label>
							<div class="frow" data-de-tierow></div>
							<input class="in" type="search" id="de-tiesearch" data-de-tiesearch autocomplete="off" placeholder="Search entities"/>
							<div class="tieres" data-de-tieres hidden></div>
							<input type="hidden" data-de-entity/>
						</div>
					</div>
					// THE LIVE PREVIEW is a client-side render of marks the payload
					// already carries — the grid chip and the Ledger row, both of
					// which ship. It resolves no audience and names no viewer.
					<div class="ed-side">
						<div class="pv" data-de-preview></div>
					</div>
				</div>
				<p class="de-err" data-de-err hidden></p>
				<div class="de-f ed-foot">
					// Delete rides the shipped DELETE's OWNER floor and nothing
					// else, and the module reveals it only in EDIT mode: a
					// `DELETE .../events/:eid` cannot name an event the POST has
					// not returned an id for, so an Owner's blank draft draws no
					// button aimed at an event that does not exist.
					if m.CanDelete {
						<button type="button" class="btn danger" data-de-delete hidden>Delete event</button>
					}
					<span class="sp"></span>
					<button type="button" class="btn" data-de-cancel>Cancel</button>
					<button type="submit" class="btn fill" data-de-save>Save changes</button>
				</div>
			</form>
		</div>
	</div>
}
